1
00:00:27,361 --> 00:00:30,964
(Francesca Next Door)

2
00:00:33,033 --> 00:00:34,635
(All names of people, places, events,
and other details are fictitious.)

3
00:00:34,701 --> 00:00:35,969
(AI-based technology was used
in part of the production.)

4
00:00:36,236 --> 00:00:40,941
<i>Sagging skin, pull it tight.</i>

5
00:00:41,008 --> 00:00:45,145
<i>Wrinkles, smooth out right.</i>

6
00:00:51,685 --> 00:00:53,787
I asked for a facelift,

7
00:00:53,854 --> 00:00:56,356
and now they're asking me
to give them a cash lift?

8
00:00:56,423 --> 00:01:00,928
Honestly, they can sniff out
my money like bloodhounds.

9
00:01:02,763 --> 00:01:03,764
What's that smell?

10
00:01:04,631 --> 00:01:07,568
- Okay, slow.
- Take it easy.

11
00:01:07,634 --> 00:01:08,969
Be careful.

12
00:01:09,536 --> 00:01:11,705
- Watch out.
- It's so heavy.

13
00:01:13,674 --> 00:01:14,908
Easy now.

14
00:01:16,910 --> 00:01:18,011
What's going on?

15
00:01:19,947 --> 00:01:21,748
Excuse me, let me through.

16
00:01:22,716 --> 00:01:25,218
Excuse me. What is that?

17
00:01:25,285 --> 00:01:27,020
I think someone died.

18
00:01:27,754 --> 00:01:29,957
Someone died?

19
00:01:31,425 --> 00:01:32,426
This way.

20
00:01:33,327 --> 00:01:34,361
Easy.

21
00:01:35,996 --> 00:01:38,632
Hey, handsome guy with a mustache.

22
00:01:38,865 --> 00:01:40,133
What is this thing?

23
00:01:40,334 --> 00:01:41,668
It belongs to the new resident here.

24
00:01:41,735 --> 00:01:43,136
I'm not sure what it is, ma'am.

25
00:01:43,203 --> 00:01:45,572
I'm sorry. "Ma'am?"

26
00:01:45,639 --> 00:01:47,374
I'm not that old!

27
00:01:47,441 --> 00:01:48,442
Fine, I'm sorry, miss.

28
00:01:48,508 --> 00:01:49,543
We'll get moving.

29
00:01:49,910 --> 00:01:51,511
Oh, my goodness.

30
00:01:51,578 --> 00:01:54,514
What is this in the rain,
a coffin-showboating situation?

31
00:01:55,349 --> 00:01:56,850
Ladies, isn't it unbelievable?

32
00:01:56,917 --> 00:01:58,752
What's happening to our neighborhood?

33
00:01:58,819 --> 00:01:59,987
- Oh, right.
- Goodness me.

34
00:02:00,053 --> 00:02:03,156
I have a very bad feeling about this.

35
00:02:06,426 --> 00:02:08,195
Oh, lightning...

36
00:02:10,230 --> 00:02:12,132
- Put it down here.
- Slowly.

37
00:02:16,403 --> 00:02:18,972
Is this person nuts?

38
00:02:19,473 --> 00:02:21,975
Who puts a coffin at home?

39
00:02:22,042 --> 00:02:24,244
Gosh, it was ridiculously heavy too.

40
00:02:24,544 --> 00:02:25,579
That's it, right?

41
00:02:25,646 --> 00:02:27,514
- Yeah, let's go. I'm starving.
- Okay.

42
00:02:30,384 --> 00:02:31,585
What's an ax doing here?

43
00:02:32,686 --> 00:02:36,256
What do I know about the psychology
of someone who keeps a coffin at home?

44
00:02:37,424 --> 00:02:38,425
Let's go.

45
00:02:42,062 --> 00:02:43,563
Hey, wait up.

46
00:02:44,931 --> 00:02:46,199
Didn't you hear something?

47
00:02:46,266 --> 00:02:47,267
What?

48
00:02:47,734 --> 00:02:49,136
What did you hear?

49
00:02:51,772 --> 00:02:53,507
Maybe I heard it wrong.

50
00:02:53,840 --> 00:02:55,075
Let's just go.

51
00:02:57,044 --> 00:02:58,845
Okay, wait for me.

52
00:02:58,912 --> 00:02:59,980
This feels wrong.

53
00:03:29,910 --> 00:03:31,111
What's going on?

54
00:03:33,880 --> 00:03:35,315
Oh, you're here.

55
00:03:35,682 --> 00:03:36,717
Come sit.

56
00:03:37,617 --> 00:03:39,319
There.

57
00:03:43,123 --> 00:03:44,758
Let's see.

58
00:03:44,825 --> 00:03:46,126
(Name, Jang U Ju
Career Interests, Doctor)

59
00:03:46,193 --> 00:03:47,928
So your career interests are...

60
00:03:48,361 --> 00:03:50,263
neurosurgeon as first choice,

61
00:03:50,330 --> 00:03:51,965
OB-GYN as second choice,

62
00:03:52,199 --> 00:03:54,234
and orthopedic surgeon as third choice.

63
00:03:54,301 --> 00:03:58,572
You're determined to fix
whatever's wrong with people.

64
00:04:01,041 --> 00:04:02,042
But...

65
00:04:02,876 --> 00:04:04,311
do you have to,

66
00:04:04,845 --> 00:04:06,146
no matter what,

67
00:04:06,613 --> 00:04:07,781
become a doctor?

68
00:04:10,050 --> 00:04:12,319
Yes, that's my only goal.

69
00:04:24,064 --> 00:04:27,267
- Rock, paper, scissors, shoot!
- Rock, paper, scissors, shoot!

70
00:04:29,503 --> 00:04:32,539
But you know...

71
00:04:32,606 --> 00:04:35,776
your grades are a bit short
of med school standards.

72
00:04:36,309 --> 00:04:39,479
"Contradict" means to disagree with...

73
00:04:39,546 --> 00:04:42,115
"Contradict..."

74
00:04:42,716 --> 00:04:45,051
"Stick to" means to follow...

75
00:04:45,118 --> 00:04:46,386
Hey, don't throw it!

76
00:04:58,331 --> 00:04:59,399
Sorry, class president.

77
00:04:59,933 --> 00:05:01,134
I told you not to.

78
00:05:04,738 --> 00:05:08,542
"Be patient" means to keep your cool...

79
00:05:13,547 --> 00:05:17,184
"Be patient" means to keep your cool...

80
00:05:20,020 --> 00:05:22,255
"Tension" means stress...

81
00:05:32,399 --> 00:05:33,667
How about that?

82
00:05:34,401 --> 00:05:36,503
Really? I'm down.

83
00:05:37,237 --> 00:05:38,939
Hey, see you tomorrow.

84
00:05:39,372 --> 00:05:40,373
See you.

85
00:05:41,007 --> 00:05:42,008
Bye, class president.

86
00:05:42,275 --> 00:05:43,276
Bye, guys.

87
00:06:07,968 --> 00:06:09,970
(Hart)

88
00:06:23,617 --> 00:06:25,151
(Confused means puzzled
Panic means to be overwhelmed...)

89
00:07:03,290 --> 00:07:04,291
What the heck?

90
00:07:04,691 --> 00:07:06,726
What was that girl's deal?

91
00:07:09,963 --> 00:07:11,064
Wait.

92
00:07:11,131 --> 00:07:12,232
My vocab notebook!

93
00:07:18,838 --> 00:07:20,840
(Hart)

94
00:07:49,436 --> 00:07:53,306
<i>Happy birthday to me.</i>

95
00:07:54,774 --> 00:07:58,345
<i>Happy birthday to me.</i>

96
00:08:00,513 --> 00:08:03,283
<i>Happy birthday, dear...</i>

97
00:08:06,820 --> 00:08:09,155
<i>Happy birthday, dear...</i>

98
00:08:10,123 --> 00:08:11,491
(Dad)

99
00:08:15,996 --> 00:08:16,997
Hi, Dad.

100
00:08:17,397 --> 00:08:19,065
Hi, U Ju. It's me.

101
00:08:19,499 --> 00:08:21,634
It's morning here. What time is it there?

102
00:08:22,736 --> 00:08:23,803
It's late at night.

103
00:08:23,870 --> 00:08:25,472
Oh, I see.

104
00:08:25,538 --> 00:08:26,973
How's everything?

105
00:08:27,040 --> 00:08:29,109
The kids here are really nice.

106
00:08:29,309 --> 00:08:31,077
I don't know where they learned Korean,

107
00:08:31,144 --> 00:08:34,447
but last time,
they even thanked me in Korean.

108
00:08:34,714 --> 00:08:36,149
- Aren't they adorable?
- Right.

109
00:08:36,816 --> 00:08:37,817
I see.

110
00:08:38,151 --> 00:08:39,219
Anyway,

111
00:08:39,285 --> 00:08:42,689
you can use the card I gave you
as much as you like.

112
00:08:42,756 --> 00:08:43,790
Got it?

113
00:08:43,857 --> 00:08:45,125
So no news from you?

114
00:08:45,892 --> 00:08:48,061
- By the way, today is my...
- Okay, I'm coming.

115
00:08:48,461 --> 00:08:50,830
Sorry, I've got an emergency patient.

116
00:08:51,197 --> 00:08:52,766
I'll call you later.

117
00:08:52,832 --> 00:08:54,134
Take it easy with your studies.

118
00:08:54,601 --> 00:08:56,036
- Bye.
- Wait...

119
00:09:13,887 --> 00:09:15,722
My parents are both doctors,

120
00:09:15,789 --> 00:09:17,624
and they're overseas
providing medical aid.

121
00:09:18,291 --> 00:09:21,027
Dad is in Uganda, and Mom is in Cambodia.

122
00:09:24,464 --> 00:09:26,232
They have all this compassion
for humanity,

123
00:09:26,299 --> 00:09:28,601
but not much for their own child.

124
00:09:32,739 --> 00:09:34,808
My older sister, who's already a doctor,

125
00:09:34,874 --> 00:09:37,110
my older brother, who recently became one,
have joined them,

126
00:09:40,547 --> 00:09:42,382
Thanks to that, I'm always alone at home.

127
00:09:48,521 --> 00:09:51,658
I live alone in this big house.

128
00:09:55,562 --> 00:09:57,497
"Take it easy with your studies?"

129
00:09:59,966 --> 00:10:02,068
I must go to med school
to become a doctor.

130
00:10:02,502 --> 00:10:03,636
And to get into med school...

131
00:10:03,937 --> 00:10:05,238
I have to study.

132
00:11:03,096 --> 00:11:04,964
(Alarm)

133
00:11:07,867 --> 00:11:11,004
(Dooil High School)

134
00:11:19,179 --> 00:11:20,246
What did you do yesterday?

135
00:11:20,780 --> 00:11:21,781
You didn't text back.

136
00:11:21,848 --> 00:11:23,850
Did you hear about the new student?

137
00:11:24,217 --> 00:11:25,218
A foreigner, apparently.

138
00:11:25,285 --> 00:11:26,619
- Really? A guy?
- Yeah.

139
00:11:27,220 --> 00:11:28,288
No, it's a girl.

140
00:11:30,156 --> 00:11:31,624
Jeez, look at you.

141
00:11:31,691 --> 00:11:34,327
I saw you sleeping.
I can't deal with you guys.

142
00:11:34,394 --> 00:11:36,362
All right.

143
00:11:37,230 --> 00:11:39,732
We have a new student today.

144
00:11:40,466 --> 00:11:41,467
I'll bring her in.

145
00:11:41,734 --> 00:11:42,735
Come in.

146
00:11:56,783 --> 00:11:57,884
That girl is...

147
00:12:05,992 --> 00:12:08,394
Why, class president?
Do you have something to say?

148
00:12:09,796 --> 00:12:10,797
Sorry?

149
00:12:13,733 --> 00:12:15,702
No, sir. Never mind.

150
00:12:15,768 --> 00:12:17,503
Goodness me.

151
00:12:18,571 --> 00:12:20,707
Okay, so...

152
00:12:20,773 --> 00:12:22,242
Isn't she the weird girl from last night?

153
00:12:23,042 --> 00:12:24,410
So she was a new student?

154
00:12:25,111 --> 00:12:27,847
(Pi Na Young)

155
00:12:28,448 --> 00:12:31,751
Her name is Pi Na Young.

156
00:12:32,418 --> 00:12:34,254
She hasn't been living in Korea.

157
00:12:34,320 --> 00:12:36,122
She came from Romania.

158
00:12:36,623 --> 00:12:39,492
She may not be used to the Korean culture,

159
00:12:39,559 --> 00:12:41,894
so help her out. Understand?

160
00:12:41,961 --> 00:12:43,663
- Yes, sir!
- Okay, great.

161
00:12:44,230 --> 00:12:46,032
Let's see.

162
00:12:46,266 --> 00:12:47,600
You see that empty seat?

163
00:12:47,667 --> 00:12:48,768
Sit over there.

164
00:12:50,136 --> 00:12:51,137
Na Young?

165
00:12:53,106 --> 00:12:54,240
Who's Na Young?

166
00:12:55,541 --> 00:12:56,542
That's you.

167
00:12:56,609 --> 00:12:58,311
Take that seat over there.

168
00:12:59,279 --> 00:13:00,346
Right, I forgot.

169
00:13:01,047 --> 00:13:02,282
That was my name.

170
00:13:02,815 --> 00:13:04,751
Well, thanks, man.

171
00:13:09,789 --> 00:13:11,357
- "Thanks, man?"
- Well...

172
00:13:11,424 --> 00:13:12,825
Okay, now.

173
00:13:13,726 --> 00:13:15,895
The mock exam is just around the corner.

174
00:13:15,962 --> 00:13:18,164
That means the CSAT is coming up soon.

175
00:13:19,132 --> 00:13:20,500
You all need to study.

176
00:13:21,134 --> 00:13:22,402
Get ready for class.

177
00:13:22,935 --> 00:13:23,936
What did you say?

178
00:13:24,537 --> 00:13:25,571
One whole year left?

179
00:13:25,638 --> 00:13:28,007
That's not enough time
to bring up your grades.

180
00:13:28,608 --> 00:13:31,577
Hurry up and open your books, everyone.

181
00:13:37,216 --> 00:13:39,552
Whatever she is, I won't get involved.

182
00:13:43,656 --> 00:13:46,893
Korean verse is divided into the opening,
the middle, and the closing.

183
00:13:49,195 --> 00:13:52,465
The closing typically starts
with three syllables.

184
00:13:52,532 --> 00:13:54,767
Standard Korean verse is...

185
00:13:54,834 --> 00:13:56,302
What's the matter?

186
00:13:57,270 --> 00:13:59,172
Hey, do you know me?

187
00:14:00,173 --> 00:14:02,041
No. Look at the board.

188
00:14:04,677 --> 00:14:06,779
I definitely saw you somewhere.

189
00:14:09,248 --> 00:14:10,883
I look like a lot of people.

190
00:14:11,284 --> 00:14:12,685
I have a pretty generic face.

191
00:14:13,086 --> 00:14:14,787
So will you look at the board now?

192
00:14:15,455 --> 00:14:17,824
It's part of the closing structure.

193
00:14:20,827 --> 00:14:21,894
New student?

194
00:14:22,428 --> 00:14:24,630
You should focus on me during class.

195
00:14:28,935 --> 00:14:29,936
Fine.

196
00:14:32,004 --> 00:14:34,874
Anyway, this is a frequently tested topic.
Keep that in mind.

197
00:14:34,941 --> 00:14:37,110
You should always aim to get
one more question right.

198
00:14:39,579 --> 00:14:40,747
Maybe not.

199
00:15:00,967 --> 00:15:03,069
- I'll see you next class.
- Thank you, sir.

200
00:15:03,569 --> 00:15:05,671
Class is over, so...

201
00:15:35,435 --> 00:15:36,903
You're from Romania,

202
00:15:36,969 --> 00:15:38,571
but you speak pretty good Korean.

203
00:15:39,205 --> 00:15:40,873
Didn't you learn to be polite, though?

204
00:15:41,140 --> 00:15:43,876
That's only for people above me.

205
00:15:43,943 --> 00:15:45,311
Who's above me in this place?

206
00:15:48,948 --> 00:15:50,483
You're funny.

207
00:15:51,717 --> 00:15:52,752
But hear me out.

208
00:15:53,219 --> 00:15:54,887
There's a hierarchy in school.

209
00:15:55,688 --> 00:15:57,256
Let me make one thing clear.

210
00:15:57,857 --> 00:15:59,325
I'm certainly above you...

211
00:15:59,392 --> 00:16:01,027
Gosh, what the heck?

212
00:16:02,161 --> 00:16:03,162
By any chance,

213
00:16:03,863 --> 00:16:05,264
did you just crawl out of a field?

214
00:16:05,698 --> 00:16:08,634
Excuse me, what did you say?

215
00:16:08,968 --> 00:16:10,803
You smell like grass.

216
00:16:12,972 --> 00:16:14,607
Okay, that's it. I've had it.

217
00:16:17,977 --> 00:16:19,612
This is Diptyque.

218
00:16:19,679 --> 00:16:21,247
It's super expensive!

219
00:16:21,948 --> 00:16:23,049
Really?

220
00:16:23,115 --> 00:16:24,116
You like the smell of grass?

221
00:16:24,183 --> 00:16:25,351
Interesting taste.

222
00:16:25,985 --> 00:16:29,021
Great, I'll start calling you "Grass."

223
00:16:30,723 --> 00:16:32,258
Nice to meet you, Grass.

224
00:16:34,794 --> 00:16:37,363
- She definitely doesn't know who I am.
- She has no clue.

225
00:16:37,430 --> 00:16:38,831
Are you crazy?

226
00:16:41,734 --> 00:16:43,102
That's a rough way to say hello.

227
00:16:45,404 --> 00:16:46,873
Pleasure to meet you, Grass.

228
00:16:47,874 --> 00:16:49,275
Why are you just standing there, A Ra?

229
00:16:49,709 --> 00:16:51,177
You're out of your mind.

230
00:16:55,581 --> 00:16:57,183
Okay, nice to meet you as well.

231
00:16:59,252 --> 00:17:01,454
I want to greet you too,
but I'm out of hands.

232
00:17:01,521 --> 00:17:02,522
Will you wait a minute?

233
00:17:03,222 --> 00:17:04,323
Hold on.

234
00:17:04,390 --> 00:17:07,260
My scalp is bleeding, Na Young.

235
00:17:07,326 --> 00:17:09,095
Okay, I let go. Let's talk it out.

236
00:17:09,161 --> 00:17:11,230
Please, I'm sorry.

237
00:17:11,297 --> 00:17:13,332
- I already let go.
- Please let go.

238
00:17:13,399 --> 00:17:16,602
Never get involved.

239
00:17:18,437 --> 00:17:19,906
Never get involved.

240
00:17:20,039 --> 00:17:21,040
I'm sorry?

241
00:17:21,107 --> 00:17:22,675
My point is...

242
00:17:23,976 --> 00:17:25,811
You should look out for her.

243
00:17:26,012 --> 00:17:27,914
As the class president, got it?

244
00:17:29,215 --> 00:17:31,083
- But...
- You saw her.

245
00:17:31,150 --> 00:17:33,386
She doesn't even know
how to speak politely.

246
00:17:33,986 --> 00:17:36,355
Help her adjust to life in Korea.

247
00:17:37,256 --> 00:17:38,891
Help her find her way around,

248
00:17:39,191 --> 00:17:41,460
and do your part as the class president.

249
00:17:41,861 --> 00:17:44,397
Okay, I'll do that.

250
00:17:44,463 --> 00:17:45,464
Good.

251
00:17:47,500 --> 00:17:48,501
Please do.

252
00:17:52,738 --> 00:17:54,173
Where's Na Young?

253
00:17:54,240 --> 00:17:55,241
What?

254
00:17:57,076 --> 00:17:58,077
I don't know.

255
00:18:00,012 --> 00:18:01,614
Where did she go?

256
00:18:06,319 --> 00:18:07,520
What the heck? You startled me!

257
00:18:07,954 --> 00:18:10,423
Hey, why are you in there?

258
00:18:10,923 --> 00:18:12,325
This is more comfortable.

259
00:18:12,391 --> 00:18:14,093
It feels cozy and familiar.

260
00:18:14,393 --> 00:18:15,861
Well, okay. Anyway...

261
00:18:17,163 --> 00:18:18,931
If you're stuck with something,

262
00:18:18,998 --> 00:18:20,967
just come to me and ask me about it.

263
00:18:22,702 --> 00:18:23,703
Ask you?

264
00:18:25,071 --> 00:18:26,072
Why?

265
00:18:27,473 --> 00:18:29,141
So it's because...

266
00:18:31,043 --> 00:18:32,545
I'm the class president.

267
00:18:33,379 --> 00:18:34,380
Class president?

268
00:18:34,447 --> 00:18:37,049
All right, folks. Sit down.

269
00:18:38,684 --> 00:18:40,720
Let's talk later.

270
00:18:42,421 --> 00:18:45,157
You'll take a short quiz today.

271
00:18:45,891 --> 00:18:48,227
It shouldn't be too hard
since we've covered all this.

272
00:18:48,294 --> 00:18:51,664
- But it's not fair.
- We're not ready yet.

273
00:18:51,731 --> 00:18:52,732
What are you doing?

274
00:18:56,369 --> 00:18:57,803
Here you go.

275
00:19:06,612 --> 00:19:07,813
Hey.

276
00:19:08,381 --> 00:19:09,482
Hey.

277
00:19:10,750 --> 00:19:12,051
Pass me the...

278
00:19:24,263 --> 00:19:26,198
- Hey, teacher.
- What?

279
00:19:26,465 --> 00:19:28,734
What's the answer to the first question?

280
00:19:29,201 --> 00:19:30,269
What?

281
00:19:31,737 --> 00:19:33,739
What do you think you're doing?

282
00:19:34,006 --> 00:19:36,108
This is a quiz.

283
00:19:40,046 --> 00:19:42,715
Isn't it a teacher's job to teach us
what we don't know?

284
00:19:42,782 --> 00:19:44,784
Well, that's right,

285
00:19:44,850 --> 00:19:46,452
but you're taking a quiz.

286
00:19:47,653 --> 00:19:48,654
Is that right?

287
00:19:49,121 --> 00:19:50,122
Too bad.

288
00:19:52,291 --> 00:19:53,292
Hey, class president.

289
00:19:55,695 --> 00:19:57,563
What's the answer?

290
00:19:59,465 --> 00:20:01,600
You're asking me now?

291
00:20:02,034 --> 00:20:04,036
You told me to ask you
if I was stuck with something.

292
00:20:18,284 --> 00:20:20,453
You can't ask about answers to a quiz.

293
00:20:27,793 --> 00:20:29,695
Where is her common sense?

294
00:20:30,096 --> 00:20:31,430
She's got absolutely no manners.

295
00:20:32,932 --> 00:20:35,434
Let's just get through today.

296
00:20:36,769 --> 00:20:39,038
I'll just show her the basics
and get it over with.

297
00:20:43,375 --> 00:20:44,376
Hey.

298
00:20:44,677 --> 00:20:46,345
Don't you have any cash on you?

299
00:20:46,645 --> 00:20:48,180
I really don't.

300
00:20:48,748 --> 00:20:51,350
Every dime I find on you
earns you a smack.

301
00:20:51,784 --> 00:20:55,221
Wait, that phrase is ancient, isn't it?

302
00:20:55,287 --> 00:20:57,556
Who carries around cash these days?

303
00:20:57,923 --> 00:21:01,093
You see, we accept mobile transfers.

304
00:21:01,460 --> 00:21:03,229
I'd prefer a fee-free option.

305
00:21:03,295 --> 00:21:04,363
What do you think?

306
00:21:04,697 --> 00:21:06,499
What are you even...

307
00:21:07,199 --> 00:21:08,400
What do you say?

308
00:21:20,513 --> 00:21:23,449
It's the law of nature
for the strong to prey on the weak.

309
00:21:23,983 --> 00:21:24,984
Keep going.

310
00:21:26,886 --> 00:21:28,587
Who the heck are you?

311
00:21:28,654 --> 00:21:30,556
Isn't that the freaky new student?

312
00:21:31,290 --> 00:21:32,825
Oh, the one from Romania...

313
00:21:33,359 --> 00:21:35,928
But you look way too Korean.

314
00:21:35,995 --> 00:21:37,096
So what?

315
00:21:37,163 --> 00:21:39,732
Should I teach you a lesson?

316
00:21:43,936 --> 00:21:45,104
What was that?

317
00:22:07,393 --> 00:22:08,394
Hey.

318
00:22:12,898 --> 00:22:14,767
Who are you now?

319
00:22:18,437 --> 00:22:19,438
Hi, Hyeol.

320
00:22:22,141 --> 00:22:24,710
Now who do you think you are?

321
00:22:25,377 --> 00:22:26,979
You've got something to say to my friend?

322
00:22:27,046 --> 00:22:28,314
Not at all.

323
00:22:29,648 --> 00:22:31,517
Why are you scared? Who's this guy?

324
00:22:31,584 --> 00:22:33,819
Jeez, don't you know Bloody Yoo Hyeol?

325
00:22:35,955 --> 00:22:37,890
Oh, shoot. Is that him?

326
00:22:37,957 --> 00:22:39,291
Will you answer my question? Who is he?

327
00:22:39,358 --> 00:22:40,993
We have to get out of here.

328
00:22:41,060 --> 00:22:42,962
Here's all my cash.

329
00:22:43,028 --> 00:22:45,698
I can even transfer you some money.

330
00:22:45,764 --> 00:22:47,833
- We have to go!
- Why?

331
00:22:47,900 --> 00:22:49,335
- Let's go.
- Wait, but...

332
00:22:49,401 --> 00:22:50,870
- Hey...
- Bye, guys.

333
00:22:50,936 --> 00:22:52,838
Who the heck is he?

334
00:22:54,240 --> 00:22:55,241
Bye.

335
00:22:58,344 --> 00:23:00,512
I don't have a friend like you.

336
00:23:01,113 --> 00:23:02,114
I know.

337
00:23:02,481 --> 00:23:04,149
So let's be friends starting today.

338
00:23:06,719 --> 00:23:08,520
We'll be pretty good friends.

339
00:23:09,054 --> 00:23:10,055
Don't you think?

340
00:23:15,327 --> 00:23:16,328
Pi Na Young.

341
00:23:18,497 --> 00:23:19,498
Class president?

342
00:23:20,966 --> 00:23:23,502
I told you to wait in your seat.
When did you come out?

343
00:23:23,736 --> 00:23:25,437
Follow me.
I'll show you around the school.

344
00:23:36,949 --> 00:23:39,618
I'll give you
a step-by-step tour of the facilities,

345
00:23:39,919 --> 00:23:40,920
so for now...

346
00:23:44,790 --> 00:23:46,091
Why do you have that?

347
00:23:46,325 --> 00:23:47,493
I like the color red.

348
00:23:47,860 --> 00:23:49,295
I like everything red.

349
00:23:49,695 --> 00:23:51,297
I like this one. I'll take it.

350
00:23:51,363 --> 00:23:52,364
I like how it hugs me.

351
00:23:52,865 --> 00:23:54,033
Put it back.

352
00:23:56,168 --> 00:23:57,169
What's this?

353
00:23:57,603 --> 00:23:58,604
Is this a ring?

354
00:23:58,971 --> 00:23:59,972
Wait, hold on.

355
00:24:06,345 --> 00:24:07,413
Hey, miss.

356
00:24:09,615 --> 00:24:10,616
Hey.

357
00:24:11,083 --> 00:24:12,318
You have to pay for those.

358
00:24:14,653 --> 00:24:16,388
- Enjoy.
- Thank you.

359
00:24:20,259 --> 00:24:22,361
You have to line up.

360
00:24:37,242 --> 00:24:38,477
(The Private Lives of Vampires)

361
00:24:41,080 --> 00:24:42,982
Hush. You have to be silent.

362
00:24:45,451 --> 00:24:47,152
I didn't get to study at all.

363
00:24:47,820 --> 00:24:49,688
School is so annoying.

364
00:24:49,755 --> 00:24:51,323
There are way too many rules.

365
00:24:53,225 --> 00:24:55,294
I know you're not from here,
but there's a limit.

366
00:24:55,794 --> 00:24:57,830
Didn't anyone teach you basic decency?

367
00:24:58,564 --> 00:24:59,865
What are you, really?

368
00:25:00,499 --> 00:25:01,500
Me?

369
00:25:02,901 --> 00:25:04,870
Do you want to know?

370
00:25:08,474 --> 00:25:09,475
I'm a...

371
00:25:20,619 --> 00:25:21,620
I'm a human being.

372
00:25:22,287 --> 00:25:23,622
That's for sure!

373
00:25:31,964 --> 00:25:33,365
Okay, this is it.

374
00:25:33,966 --> 00:25:34,967
What is?

375
00:25:36,201 --> 00:25:37,836
We're outside of school
from this point on.

376
00:25:38,570 --> 00:25:41,306
I'm only responsible for you
on school grounds.

377
00:25:41,373 --> 00:25:42,975
Outside, you're on your own.

378
00:25:44,243 --> 00:25:46,545
So let's call it a day today.

379
00:25:46,612 --> 00:25:47,613
Bye.

380
00:26:03,328 --> 00:26:04,329
What's going on?

381
00:26:05,431 --> 00:26:06,432
What?

382
00:26:06,799 --> 00:26:08,100
Why are you following me?

383
00:26:08,400 --> 00:26:09,735
I'm not following you.

384
00:26:41,166 --> 00:26:42,201
Are you kidding me?

385
00:26:43,035 --> 00:26:44,036
What do you mean?

386
00:26:44,503 --> 00:26:45,804
You are following me.

387
00:26:45,871 --> 00:26:46,939
I'm not.

388
00:26:49,808 --> 00:26:51,777
Fine, which way is your place?

389
00:26:52,111 --> 00:26:53,112
My place?

390
00:26:53,312 --> 00:26:54,313
That way.

391
00:26:54,947 --> 00:26:55,948
(Dalbit-ro)

392
00:27:08,994 --> 00:27:10,496
I bet she's gone by now.

393
00:27:10,829 --> 00:27:12,931
Jeez, why do I have to deal with her mess?

394
00:27:13,799 --> 00:27:15,567
I wasted so much time to chase her off.

395
00:27:16,568 --> 00:27:17,903
I'll hurry back home and study.

396
00:27:20,806 --> 00:27:21,807
Oh, no.

397
00:27:44,062 --> 00:27:45,697
Where's my phone?

398
00:27:54,840 --> 00:27:55,874
Na Young?

399
00:29:00,105 --> 00:29:02,207
How did you just...

400
00:29:12,884 --> 00:29:15,887
(Francesca Next Door)

401
00:31:16,375 --> 00:31:18,377
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
